[h1]Auto Theme[/h1]
[b]Preview 0.2.4 · Single-player only · Partial in-game checks; full validation pending[/b]

Arrange all standard Great Works slots, including relics, writing, music and corporation products.

[h2]How to use[/h2]
Open the Great Works window and click Arrange Great Works during your turn. Preserve existing themes; form new themes first, then improve supported placements. Bounded heuristics do not guarantee an optimal result.

The compact toolbar shows the current themed-building count and status. Pillaged collections, art cooldowns and incomplete archaeology museums receive specific explanations; manual changes and repairs refresh availability. A shuffled 24-work test collection recovered five themes in three native swaps after repairing pillaged test buildings, with IDs and count preserved.

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
The target setup is Gathering Storm with Harmony in Diversity. Partial real-game checks were performed in one user HD collection; full feature and compatibility validation remains pending. Multiplayer and hotseat are unsupported. Avoid assigning the same objects to another automation mod.

[h2]Feedback[/h2]
Include game/DLC/HD versions, enabled mods, reproduction steps and relevant Lua.log or Modding.log errors.

[h2]Credits[/h2]
xuanda0201. Original code and cover layout: MIT. Game screenshots and game content remain the property of their respective rights holders. Not an official Firaxis, 2K, Aspyr or HD release.

[h2]Installation[/h2]
Subscribe, wait for Steam to finish downloading, then enable Auto Theme under Additional Content → Mods. Remove a local AutoTheme copy with the same mod ID before using the Workshop version.

